msgid "Radar"
msgstr "Radar"

msgid ""
"Radar has no analytics, no cookies, no accounts and no advertising. Your "
"choices and anything you save stay in this browser: your saved items, the "
"identities you viewed (off unless you turn it on), the names you gave, your "
"settings and devnets, and a cache of recent answers so pages open quickly. A"
" service worker keeps Radar’s own files so it can open offline."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Radar is a read-only explorer for Dash Core, Dash Platform and the network "
"under both. It never signs, never broadcasts and never asks for a key."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Radar keeps the last 300 proofs. Load the figure again to get its proof."
msgstr ""

msgid "Radar on GitHub"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Radar only reads. To top up an identity, register a name, or work with a "
"token, a contract or a Platform address, use Bridge. To vote on a proposal "
"or as a masternode, use Governance. Each link opens in a new tab and carries"
" the network you were looking at."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Radar’s code is open source under the MIT licence. Where it adapts code or "
"data from another project, that project is listed here and in the file it "
"lives in. Libraries installed through npm and cargo keep their own licences."
msgstr ""

